Refactor this function so that it reads the file once, handles a missing file by returning an empty dict, and has type hints. Show only the new code.

```python
def load(path):
    counts = {}
    for line in open(path).readlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if line == '':
            continue
        word = line.split(',')[0]
        if word in counts:
            counts[word] = counts[word] + 1
        else:
            counts[word] = 1
    for line in open(path).readlines():
        if line.startswith('#'):
            print('comment', line)
    return counts
